  "question": {
    "text": "The condition for a reaction to occur spontaneously is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\Delta H$ must be negative",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\Delta S$ must be negative",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$(\\Delta H-T \\Delta S)$ must be negative",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$(\\Delta H+T \\Delta S)$ must be negative",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "For a spontaneous reaction, $\\Delta G$ = negative and $\\Delta S=$ positive\r\n$$\r\n\\Delta G=\\Delta H-T \\Delta S=-v e\r\n$$\r\nHence, $\\Delta H-T \\Delta S=-$ ve only when $\\Delta S=+$ ve and\r\n$$\r\n\\Delta H=-v e\r\n$$"
